      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: If `chain.size() \u003e 1`, this will output `if (head)\u0027s else`, dropping the intermediate `else if` conditions (e.g., an `if (A) { ... } else if (B) { ... } else { ... }` will result in `if (A)\u0027s else` instead of something indicating `B` was involved).\n\nConsider using `chain.back()` for the `else` clause when the chain is longer than 1:\n```cpp\nif (chain.size() \u003d\u003d 1) {\n  clauses.push_back(\"if (\" + head + \")\u0027s else\");\n} else {\n  clauses.push_back(\"if (\" + head + \")\u0027s else if (\" +\n                    get_condition_text(chain.back()) + \")\u0027s else\");\n}\n```\nThis would change the output for `generic.cc` in your tests to `if (is_win)\u0027s else if (is_linux)\u0027s else`, which might be a bit more descriptive.",
